@baseUrl = http://localhost:5136

### 1. Login as tom and keep the token
# @name loginTom
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/account/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userName": "tom",
  "password": "Pa$$w0rd"
}

### 2. No token → 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/photos
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----PhotoBoundary

------PhotoBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="photo.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./samples/photo.jpg
------PhotoBoundary--

### 3. Upload a JPEG → 201, isMain true the first time, false after that
# @name uploadPhoto
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/photos
Authorization: Bearer {{loginTom.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----PhotoBoundary

------PhotoBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="photo.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./samples/photo.jpg
------PhotoBoundary--

### 4. Wrong file type → 400 "Only JPEG, PNG and WebP images are allowed."
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/photos
Authorization: Bearer {{loginTom.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----PhotoBoundary

------PhotoBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="notes.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

this is not an image
------PhotoBoundary--

### 5. Set the uploaded photo as main → 204
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/photos/{{uploadPhoto.response.body.id}}/main
Authorization: Bearer {{loginTom.response.body.token}}

### 6. Photo that doesn't exist (or isn't mine) → 404
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/photos/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/main
Authorization: Bearer {{loginTom.response.body.token}}

### 7. Not a guid → 404 (route constraint, handler 

### 6. Photo that doesn't exist (or isn't mine) → 404
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/photos/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/main
Authorization: Bearer {{loginTom.response.body.token}}

### 7. Not a guid → 404 (route constraint, handler never runs)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/photos/abc/main
Authorization: Bearer {{loginTom.response.body.token}}

### 8. Get the uploaded file straight from storage → 200 (the image)
GET {{uploadPhoto.response.body.url}}

### 9. Delete the uploaded photo → 204 (or 409 if it's the main photo)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/photos/{{uploadPhoto.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginTom.response.body.token}}

### 10. Get the same file again → 404, it's gone from storage
GET {{uploadPhoto.response.body.url}}

### 11. Delete it again → 404, the row is gone too
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/photos/{{uploadPhoto.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginTom.response.body.token}}